 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Use the data in <a href=\"https://openstax.org/r/Chapter8_Data-Sets\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">“WNBA2019”</a> to answer these questions about the relationship between the proportion of made field goals (FG%) and the proportion of made three-point field goals (3P%):",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 542803,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the equation of the regression line for proportion of made three-point field goals vs. proportion of made field goals?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In Google Sheets, highlight the data including the headers.</p>\n<p>Open a copy of the file in Google Sheets. You cannot edit the original file.</p>\n<p>Look for the WNBA2019 tab.</p>\n<p>It will be easier for Google to suggest what you want if your columns are adjacent. First create a blank column to the right of the column FG%. Then copy the column 3P% into the blank column.</p>\n<p>Highlight the columns for FG% and 3P% (including the headers).</p>\n<p>Choose Insert, then choose Chart.</p>\n<p>It may suggest a line chart in “Chart type.”</p>\n<p>In the Chart type drop down box, choose a scatter plot.</p>\n<p>Make sure that FG% is on the horizontal axis.</p>\n<p>Once you have the scatter plot, Google Sheets can generate the regression line by clicking the three dots at the top right of the plot.</p>\n<p>Then select “Edit chart.”</p>\n<p>Then click on “Customize” and “Series.”</p>\n<p>Then add the regression line by checking the box next to “Trendline.”</p>\n<p>Show the equation by selection “Use Equation” in the drop-down menu under “Label.”</p>\n<p>The equation appears on the graph: 0.548*<i>x</i> + 0.106</p>\n<p>The “<i>y</i> = ” is implied.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y{\\text{ }} = 0.548x\\; + {\\text{ }}0.106\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = 0.5481x + 0.1055\">y = 0.5481x + 0.1055</span>, where x is the proportion of made field goals and y is the proportion of made three-point field goals"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 542804,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What proportion of made three-point field goals would we expect for a team that makes 44% of its field goals?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.347"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Use the equation, <span data-math=\"y{\\text{ }} = 0.548x\\; + {\\text{ }}0.106\"></span>, where <i>x</i> is the proportion of field goals and <i>y</i> is the proportion of three-point field goals.</p>\n<p>Substitute 0.44 for <i>x</i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.548\\left( {0.44} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}0.106{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}0.347\"></span></p>\n<p>You would expect a proportion of 0.347.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 542805,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Did the Dallas Wings overperform or underperform in terms of proportion of made three-point field goals, based on the team’s proportion of made field goals?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Predicted: 0.340; actual: 0.368. The Aces made about 2.8% more of their three-point shots than expected."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 542806,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write a sentence to interpret the slope of the regression line.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The regression equation is <span data-math=\"y{\\text{ }} = 0.548x\\; + {\\text{ }}0.106\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The slope is 0.548.</p>\n<p>This tells you that an increase of one percent in the field goal attempts will result, in the long term, in an expected increase of around 55 percent in made three-point field goal attempts.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "An increase of 1% in made field goal attempts will result in an expected increase of 0.55% in made three-point field goal attempts."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
